  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Leaderboard sets organize several leaderboards into a single unit. For example, in a game that includes many levels, you might define a leaderboard set to organize the leaderboards for each level. A single app can have 100 leaderboard sets, and a set can have a maximum of 100 leaderboards. You must have at least one leaderboard for your app before you can create a leaderboard set. Once you add leaderboard sets to your app, all future leaderboards that you configure for the app must be included in a leaderboard set.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The process to start using leaderboard sets to organize your app’s leaderboards includes these steps:",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "For more information about how to use Leaderboard sets in your app, see `https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/configure-game-center/configure-leaderboard-sets`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/configure-game-center/configure-leaderboard-sets"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": [
        {
          "text": "Create the first leaderboard set.",
